# ── Genesis configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8787
GENESIS_WORKSPACE=/path/to/a/git/repo        # local host: where the agent runs
# GENESIS_WORKSPACE_NAME=root                # display label for the default workspace (blank → "genesis")
GENESIS_AGENT_ARGS=--dangerously-skip-permissions
# GENESIS_TOKEN=                              # bearer gate for /message + /threads

# ── Durable store (Phase 2) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...                 # → Postgres (Railway). Else pglite:
GENESIS_DATA_DIR=~/.genesis/data             # persistent pglite (FS-as-truth)

# ── Execution host (Phase 4) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENESIS_HOST=vercel                         # → microVM tier (Vercel Sandbox)
# Vercel auth — either OIDC (automatic on Vercel; `vercel env pull` locally):
#   VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=
# …or an access token (CI / non-Vercel):
#   VERCEL_TOKEN=
#   VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
#   VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
# Keyed creds boundary-injected into the sandbox (NOT subscription OAuth):
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Sandbox tuning:
#   GENESIS_SANDBOX_NAME=genesis-default      # continuity key (persistent VM)
#   GENESIS_GIT_URL=https://github.com/you/repo   # cloned into the VM at create
#   GENESIS_REMOTE_CWD=/vercel/sandbox        # agent working dir inside the VM
#   GENESIS_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT_MS=2700000        # 45 min
#   GENESIS_SANDBOX_BOOTSTRAP=["npm","i","-g","@anthropic-ai/claude-code"]  # JSON argv (install agent CLI)
# Egress firewall. Default = deny-by-default ALLOW-LIST (api.anthropic.com + npm),
# so the keyed agent reaches the LLM while everything else is blocked. NOTE: this
# default is narrow — tasks that git-push, clone other repos, pip-install, or call
# MCP servers need a WIDER allow-list. Widen via a JSON allow-list object:
#   GENESIS_NETWORK_POLICY={"allow":["api.anthropic.com","github.com","api.github.com","codeload.github.com","registry.npmjs.org","files.pythonhosted.org"]}
# Or "allow-all" (no isolation) / "deny-all" (blocks the LLM — agent won't run):
#   GENESIS_NETWORK_POLICY=allow-all

# ── Voice channel (BRO-2228) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# An ElevenLabs phone agent calls /voice/identify and /voice/request as webhook
# tools. UNSET GENESIS_VOICE_SECRET → the routes are NOT REGISTERED AT ALL (404),
# never "registered but open": an unconfigured deploy must not expose an intake.
# The secret is presented by ElevenLabs in the x-genesis-voice-secret header.
#   GENESIS_VOICE_SECRET=                     # REQUIRED to enable /voice/*
# Who may receive a follow-up. Comma-separated `number` or `number:Name`, same
# grammar as GENESIS_WHATSAPP_ALLOWED_USERS. Any spelling works — ids are
# normalized to digits, so "+57 301 775-8620:Carlos" matches a caller dialing in
# as 573017758620. A caller NOT listed is not rejected: they are a normal
# stranger, and the agent takes a message it cannot follow up on.
#   GENESIS_VOICE_PRINCIPALS=573017758620:Carlos,573214994114
# Where queued tickets land (append-only JSONL, consumed by the delivery leg).
#   GENESIS_VOICE_QUEUE_DIR=~/.genesis/data/voice
#
# WHY caller id is safe to route on though it is spoofable: answers are delivered
# to the number ON FILE, never to whoever is on the line. A spoofer causes the
# real owner to receive an unrequested reply — a detection, not a breach. Any
# capability WITHOUT that property (acting for the caller, reading their data
# aloud) must not be added without a second factor.
# There is NO env var for delivery, and no build() option either. Nothing in this
# tree drains the queue, so a follow-up is not merely switched off — it cannot be
# expressed: /voice/identify always answers canFollowUp:false and /voice/request
# always answers followUp:"none". The request is still RECORDED, with its delivery
# target; only the promise is withheld. The change that adds a queue-draining
# consumer is the change that restores the option, and is also the point at which
# the queue's best-effort durability (no fsync) stops being acceptable.

# Skills installed into EVERY provisioned tenant workspace, root-owned 0444.
# Read by the provisioner (root), never by a tenant — so a tenant runs with the
# skill and can never rewrite it. `.claude/` stays write-denied because
# `allowed-tools:` frontmatter is a real permission layer.
# GENESIS_TENANT_SKILLS_DIR=/home/agent/genesis/tenant-skills

# ── ElevenLabs voice agent (BRO-2257) ───────────────────────────────────
# Only needed to PROVISION the phone agent (scripts/elevenlabs-provision.sh).
# Genesis itself never calls ElevenLabs — the agent calls Genesis.
#   ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=                       # elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
#   GENESIS_PUBLIC_URL=https://host.ts.net    # base URL ElevenLabs reaches us on;
#                                             # no path, no trailing slash
# GENESIS_VOICE_SECRET is reused from the voice-channel block above and MUST
# match on both sides, or every tool call is a 401 that sounds like success.
